What are Audio ICs and Audio Amplifiers?
Audio Integrated Circuits (ICs) encompass specialized components including audio amplifiers, converters (CODECs), processors (DSPs), and complete System-on-Chip (SoC) solutions. These semiconductor devices perform critical functions like signal modulation, noise cancellation, and audio enhancement. Audio Amplifiers specifically boost low-power audio signals to drive speakers and headphones, with their performance determined by parameters like total harmonic distortion (THD), signal-to-noise ratio (SNR), and power efficiency.

